# Printer Deployment in Active Directory

## Objective

Deploy a shared network printer manually and automatically using Group Policy in a Windows Server 2022 Active Directory environment.

---

## Lab Environment

- Windows Server 2022 (Domain Controller)
- Windows 10 Client
- VMware Workstation Player
- Active Directory Domain Services
- Print and Document Services
- Group Policy Management

---

## Skills Practiced

- Installing the Print Server role
- Creating a shared printer
- Sharing printers across the network
- Deploying printers with Group Policy
- Manual printer installation
- Group Policy update
- Client verification
- Basic printer administration

---

## Printer Information

Printer Name:
HR Office Printer

Share Name:
HR-Printer

Driver:
Generic / Text Only

---

## Automatic Deployment (GPO)

The printer was deployed using:

User Configuration

Policies

Windows Settings

Deployed Printers

The printer automatically appeared on the Windows 10 client after:

gpupdate /force

and user logon.

---

## Manual Installation

The printer was also installed manually by browsing:

\\charlycyber.local

and double-clicking the shared printer.

This method is useful when installing a printer for a single user.

---

## Result

Successfully deployed a network printer to a domain user using both:

- Manual Installation
- Group Policy Deployment

---

## Lessons Learned

- Difference between manual deployment and automated deployment
- How Print Server works
- How Group Policy distributes printers
- Why organizations prefer GPO for large environments
